menu "BMDS drivers"

    config BMDS_DISPLAY_TEST_AT_BOOT
        bool "Show the display test picture from boot"
        default y
        help
            Bring-up (devplan/display.md): at boot, set the HDMI bridge up
            and start the 1280x720, 60 Hz test picture on the line-rendered
            scanout, as 'display test 720' does. It takes about 92 KB of
            internal RAM and about half of core 1 while it runs;
            'display test off' stops it. Goes away with the text console.

endmenu
